+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index, built and validated on each kiosk from the active snapshot | On-site HTTPS directory (one centrally maintained index, smaller kiosk updates); managed search service (less index maintenance, room for richer search) | Both alternatives require network connectivity at lookup time, which conflicts with the HLD tenet that lookup completes using files on the kiosk with no runtime network access. The SQLite index needs no service and gives predictable lookups, at the cost of each kiosk validating and rebuilding its own index per snapshot — a cost confined entirely to this node; the certificate interface and result are unaffected by the choice. |
